Representations. The Seller represents and warrants that:
(a) it has full legal and beneficial title to the Shares, free from all encumbrances;
(b) the Seller is duly incorporated and has the requisite power and authority to enter into this Agreement;
(c) the financial statements are accurate and prepared in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles;
(d) to the Seller’s knowledge, the Target is in compliance with applicable laws;
(e) there are no undisclosed material liabilities as of the date hereof;
(f) to the Seller’s knowledge, there is no material litigation pending or threatened against the Target; and
(g) there has been no material adverse change in the Target’s business since the date of the last financial statements provided to the Buyer.
Each of the foregoing representations and warranties is subject to disclosures in the Disclosure Schedule and shall survive Closing for a period of two (2) years, except as otherwise required by law.
